{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in `rtl/alu.sv` and extended `test/test_alu.py`.\n\nThe ADD/SUB result now uses one shared four-by-eight-bit lane. Each block\ncomputes explicitly sized nine-bit carry-zero and carry-one sums directly\nfrom its operands. Three incoming carries use expanded generate/propagate\nlookahead, and four byte selections produce the modulo-2^32 result. Only\nADD and SUB share the result-case arm. No pipeline boundaries, instruction\nlatencies, other operations, ALTOPS formulas, multiplier/divider logic,\nforwarding, address generation, branch logic, or retirement logic changed.\n\nSmall wiring details differ from the pseudocode: generate/propagate terms\nare emitted only for the lower three blocks because the final carry is\ndiscarded; the lookahead expressions reference `subtract` directly as C0.\nThe latter avoids Verilator's false UNOPTFLAT warning when public signal\nvisibility treats reads/writes of distinct bits in `carry` as a vector loop.\nNo warning or invariant check was weakened.\n\nAdded 376 directed ADD/SUB checks spanning carries/borrows at bits 8, 16,\nand 24, propagation from each lower byte, stopped propagation, zero/ones,\nsigned extremes, and overflow. Added 6,144 checks using 1,024 seeded random\noperand pairs plus equal/complemented operands, toggling ADD/SUB for each.\nAll prior arithmetic, shift, multiply, divider, and ALTOPS assertions remain.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Required Verilator lint: pass, without warnings. ALTOPS lint with public\n  signal visibility also passes.\n- Local formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed on both the initial run and the\n  final run after the C0 spelling change. No counterexamples or formal fix\n  attempts.\n- Initial full unit suite: 11 passed, two ALTOPS runner builds rejected the\n  false vector-loop warning. After fixing the wiring, the full final suite\n  passed all 13 pytest runners, including real and ALTOPS ALU/pipeline,\n  multiplier, divider, decoder, and retirement-order assertions.\n- Final `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, two ELFs including\n  retirement comparison with/without stalls and the stalled CoreMark CRC gate.\n  An initial invocation used the harness default NRET=2 and failed C++ build;\n  rerunning with the declared NRET=1 resolved the invocation mismatch.\n- Vendor timing and final `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` both measured\n  placement options 0/1/2 at 83.514, 90.117, 90.117 MHz; median 90.117 MHz.\n  All three placements succeeded. Logic 3,683, registers 1,782, LUT-RAM 0,\n  BSRAM 4, DSP 2. Placement 0's worst reported path is MEM/WB reg_write to\n  EX divider-metadata is_illegal: 17.268 ns, 12 cells. Its next path reaches\n  EX/MEM alu_result[22] through the ALU: 17.228 ns, 17 cells.\n- Final CoreMark: 10 iterations, exactly 4,416,239 marked cycles (unchanged\n  from the champion), fitness 204.06 iterations/second. The unchanged FPGA\n  gate verified canonical CRCs (seedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714, crcmatrix=1fd7,\n  crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf), the literal \"Correct operation validated.\",\n  EBREAK completion, bounded accesses, and a valid start/stop MMIO bracket.\n- Acceptance thresholds were not met: 90.117 MHz is below 103.516 MHz,\n  and 204.06 iterations/second is below the strict 234.39814 threshold.\n  This is a measured regression, not the forecast eight-percent gain.\n\nConcern: candidate-sum area and subtract/control fanout can outweigh the\nshortened carry path. Measured timing worsened and exposed control/trap paths\nalongside ALU result paths; no timing gain is claimed. The implementation\nremains the specified hypothesis for evaluation. Real M-extension RTL was\nunchanged; its unit tests and retirement cosim passed, while the slow\nformal-deep suite was not run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
