uns in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[9928 of 13000 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5e33d9ebb1b9d41b]…\n  sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\n    runner = get_runner(sim)\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\n\n    runner.build(\n        sources=[str(RTL / s) for s in sources],\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n        always=True,\n        build_args=[\"-Wall\", \"-Wno-fatal\", \"-Wno-style\"],\n    )\n    runner.test(\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        test_module=test_module,\n        test_dir=str(TEST_DIR),\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n    )\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 50.016\n  lut4: 2502\n  ff: 678\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261005-001-r2s0\n  updated: '2026-10-05T00:04:35.864040Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
