{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The core uses `nret=1`, with fetch/decode feeding the ID/EX register directly. I’ll preserve that structure and the existing memory-stall behavior. Recovery will compare the two registered EX/MEM successors only when MEM advances, so a stale prediction on a load or store waits for its request to complete.\n"}}
