{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n e=json.loads(line)\n if e.get('category')=='micro_opt' and e.get('round_id',0)>2:\n  h=e.get('hypothesis',{})\n  prose=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  print('\\\\n'+e['id']+' '+e.get('title',''))\n  print(prose)\n  print('NOTES:',e.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nhyp-20261005-001-r3s0 Share one signedness-selectable DSP multiplier across RV32M products\nReplace the three real multiplication expressions with exactly one\nsigned 33-by-33-bit multiplication whose extra operand bits encode\nsignedness. This is solely a combinational multiplier resource-sharing\noptimization; retain the champion's pipeline and execution schedule.\n\nCompute a_signed = (op == ALU_MULH || op == ALU_MULHSU) and\nb_signed = (op == ALU_MULH). Form signed 33-bit operands\nA = $signed({a_signed && a[31], a}) and\nB = $signed({b_signed && b[31], b}), and compute one signed 66-bit\nproduct P = A * B. MUL uses P[31:0]; MULH, MULHU and MULHSU share\nP[63:32] through a single grouped case arm. Zero extension for MUL\nis valid because low product bits are independent of signedness.\nKeep the sign-control gates confined to the two extension bits;\nthe original 32 data bits must feed the multiplier directly, without\noperand-wide mode muxes. Declare intermediate signedness and widths\nexplicitly so SystemVerilog expression sizing cannot truncate the\nproduct or interpret an unsigned operand as negative. Bits P[65:64]\nare intentionally unused. Avoid serial signed-correction subtractors\nor fabric-added limb products, which lengthen the measured path.\n\nGowin should map the common product into one wide DSP multiplier\ninstead of three distinct engines, removing redundant arithmetic\nblocks and simplifying the output selection and physical routing.\nPreserve every exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expression independently:\nits three add/XOR and one subtract/XOR multiply substitutes must not\nbe collapsed into the real shared product. Keep real DIV/REM in the\nexisting blocking divider. Retain all other ALU operations, decoder\nlegality, forwarding, stall and redirect priorities, memory behavior,\nnret=1 ports, RVFI source values and exactly-once ordered retirement.\n\nA temporary prototype of this exact expression and grouped high-half\nresult arm passed 20400 real multiplication checks covering directed\nedges and 5000 seeded random operand pairs\n…[32495 of 35567 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:09607311d2c9a9a7]…\nbenefit is to replace long carry propagation on the\nmeasured forwarded ALU-result path with an eight-bit local carry\npath, a small lookahead cone and a byte selection. Sharing ADD/SUB\nalso removes one wide result-selection alternative. Forecast an\nunmeasured eight percent fitness gain with medium confidence;\ncandidate-sum area, subtract-control fanout and routing may offset\nthe shorter carry path or expose a competing MEM/IF timing limit.\n\nValidate exact arithmetic with directed carry/borrow crossings at\nbits 8, 16 and 24, all-zero/all-one and signed-extreme operands,\nmodulo overflow, and seeded random ADD/SUB vectors. Run unchanged\nreal/ALTOPS pipeline, formal and retirement-cosim gates; require\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs, UART success, bounded accesses and marker\ntiming. Measure actual marked cycles and all three Gowin placement\noptions. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above\n103.516 MHz and fitness strictly above 234.39814 iter/sec. Timing\nforecasts are not measured improvements.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
