{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r4s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-001-r4s0\ntitle: \"Flatten forwarding and ALU operand selection into parallel masked muxes\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches fitness 122.36 at median Gowin Fmax 54.96 MHz\n  and 4491817 marked CoreMark cycles. Its reported 24.345 ns worst path\n  begins at MEM/WB rd and crosses forward_unit, EX operand selection,\n  and the ALU. The successful recent micro optimizations removed\n  redirect feedback and shared the multiplier, leaving late forwarding\n  control ahead of the same arithmetic. Registered multiplication\n  reached 56.203 MHz but increased cycles to 4773836 and lost fitness.\n  No recorded micro_opt attempt flattens the forwarding operand muxes;\n  LESSONS.md is absent. This is a local combinational-path optimization.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the priority-coded forwarding case muxes and the subsequent\n  ALU source muxes with explicit parallel mask-and-OR selection. Keep\n  the existing pipeline, instruction schedule, multiplier, divider,\n  memory handshakes, redirects, and nret=1 retirement boundary.\n\n  For each EX source, compute independent EX/MEM and MEM/WB destination\n  matches in parallel, including reg_write and nonzero destination.\n  Form mutually exclusive masks E = ex_match, W = wb_match && !E,\n  and R = !ex_match && !wb_match. Preserve EX/MEM precedence exactly.\n  Drive the existing two-bit forwarding interface as {W,E}: values\n  00, 01 and 10 retain their existing externally tested meanings, but\n  the EX datapath consumes the bits directly as one-hot source enables,\n  without decoding them through a priority case statement. Select raw\n  rs1 and rs2 as ORs of the three 32-bit masked sources. x0 continues\n  to come from its zero-valued register operand and never forwards.\n\n  Feed the ALU directly from a flattened selection rather than putting\n  the current is_auipc or alu_src mux after the raw forwarded rs mux.\n  For A, use pc when is_auipc, otherwise the three forwarded sources;\n  AND !is_auipc into their enables and OR the four masked data terms.\n  For B, use imm \n…[2161 of 5233 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5b27ee120b8a3192]…\ne.\n      Consume forwarding bits directly, preserve raw selected rs values\n      for every non-ALU consumer and RVFI, and leave execution timing,\n      redirects, multiplier/divider handshakes and stall logic intact.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Add focused checks for all legal forwarding selections, distinct\n      source values, AUIPC overriding forwarded A, immediate overriding\n      forwarded B, and raw rs2 preservation for stores and metadata.\n      Retain all existing divider, reset, backpressure and RVFI checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Extend directed dependencies with simultaneous matching older and\n      younger writers, both operand forwarding, x0 suppression, ALU and\n      immediate consumers, multiply/branch/store consumers, and retained\n      MEM/WB data across dmem holds. Check exact operands/results and\n      contiguous exactly-once retirement; keep every existing assertion.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
