{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r7s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Fold forwarding and operand modes into one EX selection layer\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 173.20 at median Gowin Fmax 78.418 MHz\n  and 4527646 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst path starts at a\n  registered rs2 WB dependency match and crosses EX operand selection\n  and the ALU before reaching data memory. LESSONS.md is absent.\n  Prior micro_opt experiments improved operand delivery by registering\n  dependency matches and removing PC/immediate muxes from multiplier\n  inputs. Multiplication now completes in MEM, exposing the remaining\n  serial forwarding-then-operand-mode muxes on the ordinary EX ALU path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make one local combinational optimization to EX operand steering:\n  produce mutually exclusive forwarding enables directly from the\n  existing registered dependency matches, and combine forwarding with\n  AUIPC-PC and immediate selection in a single masked-OR mux per ALU\n  operand. Preserve pipeline depth, instruction acceptance, arithmetic\n  units and latencies, bus handshakes, retirement width and cycle count.\n\n  In forward_unit, retain the four ID-aligned match registers and their\n  exact reset, flush and hold behavior. For each source, export a\n  three-bit one-hot selection in ID/EX, EX/MEM, MEM/WB order:\n  E = ex_mem_w_en && ex_match_q;\n  W = !E && mem_wb_w_en && wb_match_q;\n  I = !E && !W.\n  Use current producer controls, including EX/MEM fwd_ready and retained\n  MEM/WB ctrl.reg_write. MEM/WB valid or architectural WB w_en must not\n  qualify W: a dmem hold clears valid but keeps the producer available.\n  Preserve youngest-writer priority and zero-register exclusion.\n\n  In EX, compute raw forwarded rs1/rs2 with one-hot masked OR selection\n  for branch comparisons, JALR, stores, multiply/divide operand snapshots\n  and RVFI. Separately build ALU inputs directly from source candidates,\n  rather than feeding these raw forwarded words through another mode\n  mux. For alu_a, gate PC by is_auipc; gate all three register candidates\n\n…[2471 of 5543 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:56cd2fd65d600d53]…\n and balanced OR trees. Preserve every arithmetic,\n      branch, memory, multiply/divider snapshot and RVFI behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire direct one-hot forwarding enables from forward_unit to\n      ex_stage. Preserve all top-level ports, hazard wiring, result\n      sources, pipeline boundaries and single-channel RVFI retirement.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt standalone forwarding stimulus to the new one-hot ports.\n      Preserve all existing assertions and cover each forwarding source,\n      PC and immediate overrides with conflicting candidate values,\n      plus stores, branches, JALR and divider operand capture.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing pipeline check and verify youngest-writer\n      priority, x0, ALU/immediate consumers, forwarded address generation,\n      store data and retained-WB forwarding under long dmem holds.\n      Check identical RVFI operands/results, order and memory effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
