ved conditions. In the three valid arms XOR the selected relation with branch_op[0], implementing BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU respectively. Keep the reserved arm zero independently of the low bit. Retain branch_taken's existing is_branch qualification, all alignment traps, redirect priority, jump target/link calculations and architectural RVFI source capture. Change no decoder legality rule, ALU arithmetic, multiplier, divider or external port.\n\nAn isolated prototype of exactly this four-byte relation network and grouped predicate passed the existing EX and pipeline tests, including the existing ALTOPS schedule checks. The canonical 2K/-O3/ten-iteration CoreMark simulation with both bus stalls reached EBREAK, had no OOB access, passed all five CRCs and the required UART literal, and retained markers 15915/4543561, exactly 4,527,646 marked cycles. Vendor placement options 0/1/2 measured 81.635/85.393/85.393 MHz, versus 77.049/83.484/83.484 MHz for the champion. It uses 3265 LUTs versus 3386 with unchanged 1690 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. The worst option-0 path moves to forwarding-through-ALU result and shortens from 18.273 to 17.544 ns. The prototype median improvement is 2.29 percent, below the 4.6 percent acceptance margin; this is useful evidence but not a qualifying result. Final implementation must still pass unchanged formal and retirement cosim gates and exceed roughly 87.325 MHz at unchanged marked cycles. The intended additional gain depends on compact comparator placement and predicate sharing; confidence is low because a competing ALU path limits the measured prototype.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only the six independent branch-condition expressions with parallel eight-bit equality/less-than groups, explicit lexicographic ordering, shared signed correction and the exact two-bit relation case plus low-bit inversion. Use fully forwarded rs1/rs2; preserve reserved-condition zero, target/link arithmetic, alignment traps, redirect/reset behavior, readiness, EX/MEM holds, divider snapshots and all ALTOPS behavior.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Retain all existing assertions and add an architectural-reference branch test for all six legal predicates and both reserved conditions. Include equal operands, opposite signs, INT_MIN/INT_MAX, unsigned extremes, byte carry boundaries and seeded random pairs across all forwarding selections. Check taken/not-taken redirects, exact targets, misalignment traps and frozen EX/MEM payloads.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing tests and cover signed/unsigned boundary branches with EX/MEM and WB dependencies, both bus stalls, retained-WB forwarding, load/multiply bubbles, divider completion, wrong-path memory suppression and contiguous retirement order. Require unchanged canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker behavior and compare median vendor Fmax times actual marked iterations/cycle.'''.strip()}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Hypothesis refined and schema validation passed; further timing probes pending.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Hypothesis refined and schema validation passed; further timing probes pending.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
