{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_72", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Share one sign-extended right barrel shifter for SRL and SRA',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 184.39 iter/sec at median Gowin Fmax 83.484 MHz and 4,527,646 marked CoreMark cycles. After the dedicated effective-address lane removed ALU result selection from memory addressing, branch control and forwarded ALU results are the remaining timing limits. The ALU still expresses SRL and SRA as separate variable-shift operators and separate result arms. Sharing their data movement can reduce the ALU selection network and physical routing without spending cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; all prior micro_opt records were reviewed and none shared the right-shift network. The recent structural late-shift attempt added 1.843 percent CoreMark cycles and missed acceptance, motivating a zero-latency local implementation change.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make one local combinational resource-sharing optimization: replace the separate logical-right and arithmetic-right shift expressions with one explicitly signed 33-bit right barrel shifter. Preserve the ALU interface, EX result boundary, all instruction latencies, forwarding readiness, hazard schedule and nret=1 contract. Do not move shifts to MEM or add a shift-use stall.\n\nConstruct right_input = \"'$signed({(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31], a}) as a signed [32:0] wire. Compute exactly one signed [32:0] right_result = right_input >>> b[4:0]. Group ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA into the same case arm, assigning out = right_result[31:0]. For SRL the extra sign bit is zero, so arithmetic shifting this 33-bit nonnegative value produces the exact logical 32-bit result, including operands with bit 31 set. For SRA the extra sign bit copies a[31], so the same operator performs exact sign extension. Amounts 0 through 31 remain correct; discard only bit 32 after shifting. Keep signed declarations and the explicit signed concatenation to avoid SystemVerilog unsigned-expression mistakes.\n\nKeep SLL as its existing independent left-shift expression, and preserve every other ALU operation and all eight exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas. Do not unify left and right shifting through bit reversal: extra reversal-select muxes would enter the timed operand path. Connect the common right shifter to the current selected ALU a and b inputs, so immediate and register forms retain fully forwarded operands and AUIPC/immediate routing is unchanged. Preserve all decoder legality rules, misalignment traps, multiplier/divider arithmetic, memory enables, WB retention, redirect-over-stall priority, RVFI operands/results and strictly contiguous retirement order.\n\nAn isolated prototype containing only the stated alu.sv change passed the existing real and ALTOPS ALU tests and existing real/ALTOPS pipeline runners. Gowin placement option 0 measured 84.874 MHz versus the reproduced champion'\"'s 77.049 MHz, a 10.16 percent matched-option improvement. Its worst arrival is 17.076 ns versus 18.273 ns, with 3352 LUTs versus 3386 and unchanged 1690 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. These option-0 measurements are promising but are not the scored median; the other placement options, canonical marked CoreMark simulation and full formal checks are pending. Forecast eight percent fitness gain with medium confidence through Fmax at unchanged cycles. The principal risk is the branch/redirect path or routing limiting the final median after the ALU network shrinks. Acceptance requires fitness above 192.872 and approximately 87.325 MHz median Fmax if marked cycles stay at 4,527,646. Run every unchanged correctness and canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker gate before evaluating fitness.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add explicitly signed 33-bit right_input and right_result wires. Prepend a[31] only for ALU_SRA and zero otherwise, apply one arithmetic-right variable shift by b[4:0], and use a grouped ALU_SRL/ALU_SRA result arm selecting bits 31:0. Keep SLL independent, the same ALU ports, zero-cycle latency, every non-shift operation, defaults and exact M-extension ALTOPS substitutions.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all current assertions and extend exact SRL/SRA coverage to every amount 0..31, zero/all-one operands, INT_MIN/INT_MAX, walking bits and seeded random words. Exercise both sign-bit values and compare against an architectural 32-bit reference, including SRL with bit 31 set and SRA at amounts 0 and 31. Preserve SLL and real/ALTOPS M-extension checks.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing test and add exact-result/dependency checks for SRL/SRA/SRLI/SRAI across all shift amounts, both forwarded operand sources and register shift counts with high bits set. Exercise ALU, branch, JALR, store, multiply and divide consumers with both bus stalls and retained WB data. Assert unchanged early forwarding eligibility, no added shift-use bubble, exact RVFI source/results and contiguous order. Preserve all existing legality, alignment, memory and CoreMark validation checks.'''.strip()}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert x['id']=='hyp-20261005-001-r8s0' and x['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(x['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Shared-right-shifter hypothesis written; schema validation passed.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
