{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_84", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml');x=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nx['title']='Share an explicit five-level right-shift network for SRL and SRA'\nx['hypothesis']='''Make one local combinational resource-sharing optimization: replace the separate SRL and SRA variable-shift operators with one explicit 32-bit, five-level right-shift mux network with a common fill bit. Preserve the ALU interface, EX result boundary, instruction latencies, forwarding readiness, hazard schedule and nret=1. Do not move shifts to MEM or add a shift-use stall.\n\nSet fill = (op == ALU_SRA) && a[31]. Build these purely combinational 32-bit wires:\nshift1 = b[0] ? {fill, a[31:1]} : a;\nshift2 = b[1] ? {{2{fill}}, shift1[31:2]} : shift1;\nshift4 = b[2] ? {{4{fill}}, shift2[31:4]} : shift2;\nshift8 = b[3] ? {{8{fill}}, shift4[31:8]} : shift4;\nright_result = b[4] ? {{16{fill}}, shift8[31:16]} : shift8.\nGroup ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA into the same case arm, assigning out = right_result. All stages use the ORIGINAL operand's common fill bit; SRL fills with zero, SRA with a[31]. Use only b[4:0], so register counts are modulo 32. Amount zero returns a exactly, amount 31 produces the proper zero/sign fill, and all intermediate amounts implement exact RV32 shifting. No arithmetic-width extension, right-shift operator, sequential register or variable part select is required on this common path.\n\nKeep SLL as its current independent left-shift expression. Preserve every other ALU operation and all eight exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas. Connect the network to the current selected ALU a and b, preserving immediate/register forms and fully forwarded operands. This is one right-shifter implementation change, not a left/right reversal network or a pipeline retiming. Preserve decoder legality, all traps, multiplier/divider arithmetic, memory handshakes, WB retention, redirect-over-stall priority, RVFI operands/results and strictly contiguous retirement order.\n\nAn isolated prototype containing only this alu.sv change measured Gowin placement options 0/1 at 86.832/90.490 MHz versus the champion's 77.049/83.484 MHz. The option-0 worst arrival shortened from 18.273 to 16.811 ns, and option 1 reached 16.345 ns. Area is 3348 LUTs versus 3386, with unchanged 1690 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Option 2 is pending. The existing real/ALTOPS ALU and real/ALTOPS pipeline suites were run on this exact staged network; their final results and the exact staged-network canonical CoreMark run must be checked before treating projected fitness as measured. A related 33-bit shared-operator prototype passed all 53 unchanged ALTOPS formal checks and canonical CoreMark, but its median timing regressed; do not implement that variant or cite its correctness results as proof of this exact network.\n\nForecast eight percent fitness gain with medium confidence, from the explicit common mux network and simpler shift-result selection at unchanged marked cycles. At 90.490 MHz and 4,527,646 cycles the projection is 199.860995 iter/sec, 8.39 percent above 184.39. These prototype timing results do not replace the orchestrator's implementation and full correctness gates. Require the unchanged formal, retirement cosim and canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Acceptance needs fitness above 192.87194 and approximately 87.325 MHz median Fmax at the champion cycle count. Routing and the competing branch/ALU paths are the principal risks; preserve the specified one-bit-per-level network rather than changing block sizes or introducing extra result muxes.'''\nx['changes'][0]['description']='''Replace the two right-shift operators with a shared fill bit and the exact five combinational 32-bit mux levels shifting by 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16, selected by b[0] through b[4]. Fill each vacated region from (op == ALU_SRA) && a[31], group SRL/SRA into one result arm, and keep SLL independent. Preserve the ALU interface, zero-cycle latency, every other operation and exact ALTOPS formulas. Use explicit widths and complete assignments with no latches or extra registers.'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=80));jsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final staged-shifter hypothesis written and validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
