{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r9s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r9s0',\n'title':'Share one Boolean ALU lane for AND, OR and XOR',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 199.86 iter/sec at median Gowin Fmax 90.490 MHz and 4,527,646 marked CoreMark cycles. A reproduced option-0 report confirms competing branch-redirect and forwarded ALU-result paths at 16.811 and 16.797 ns. AND, OR and XOR currently occupy separate result-selection arms. A shared two-input Boolean lane can fit each data bit into a LUT4 and reduce the ALU result mux from three Boolean choices to one, improving placement and reducing operand fanout without spending cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; all prior micro_opt entries were reviewed. No prior hypothesis shares this Boolean lane. Isolated comparison, forwarding and redirect rewrites in this turn failed to improve the champion and are excluded.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make one combinational resource-sharing optimization in alu.sv. Form enable_ab = (op == ALU_AND || op == ALU_OR) and enable_axorb = (op == ALU_OR || op == ALU_XOR). Compute the 32-bit lane logic_result = ((a & b) & {32{enable_ab}}) | ((a \"'^ b) & {32{enable_axorb}}). Replace the three separate result arms with exactly one grouped ALU_AND, ALU_OR, ALU_XOR arm returning logic_result. The two operand bits and two enable bits give a four-input Boolean function per result bit. AND enables only the common-one term, XOR enables only the differing-bit term, and OR enables both disjoint terms. Keep the existing exact opcode case to select this lane, so all other opcodes and the zero default retain their current behavior. Add no ALU input mux, register, extra stage or vendor primitive.\n\nPreserve every other ALU operation, including the champion'\"'s exact five-level shared SRL/SRA network, independent SLL, ADD/SUB, SLT/SLTU, LUI and all eight exact ALTOPS formulas. Keep the selected a/b inputs, fully forwarded architectural operands, early-result eligibility, pipeline latencies, hazard schedule and branch penalty unchanged. Keep multiply/divide arithmetic, traps, decoder default-illegal discipline, memory handshakes, WB retention after valid clears, redirect-over-stall priority, nret=1 ports, RVFI sources/results and contiguous retirement order. Modify no evaluator files or invariant checks.\n\nAn isolated prototype of this exact grouped lane measured placement option 1 at 90.954 MHz with 3297 LUTs, 1690 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs, versus champion option 1 at 90.490 MHz and 3348 LUTs. Its worst arrival was 16.289 ns. This 0.51 percent clock gain is below acceptance and is not a completed fitness measurement. Two equivalent control formulations and the XOR merge of the disjoint terms are being checked to select a single better Boolean-lane implementation; the final file will specify only the chosen one. Forecast a five percent fitness improvement with low confidence. Routing and the competing redirect path may cap gains. Require the unchanged formal, unit, retirement-cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker gates, and all three vendor placement options. At unchanged 4,527,646 cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 94.652 MHz and fitness strictly above 209.05356. Do not treat the preliminary result as an accepted improvement.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Implement the exact shared common-one/differing-bit Boolean lane and grouped AND/OR/XOR case described above. Preserve ports, all other result arms and exact ALTOPS expressions, with complete combinational assignments and no new state. Keep the opcode gating around the shared lane so its internal values on other operations cannot affect architectural outputs.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all assertions and extend AND/OR/XOR coverage to every one-bit input truth-table combination across walking bits, zero/all-one and alternating operands, plus seeded random 32-bit pairs and operation transitions. Check against independent Python &, | and \"'^ references in both real and ALTOPS builds; retain every arithmetic and shift check.'\"'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain existing checks and add immediate/register Boolean sequences with back-to-back dependent AND/OR/XOR operations, both forwarding sources, x0, store/branch/JALR/MUL/DIV consumers, both bus stalls and long retained-WB holds. Assert unchanged early forwarding and no added bubbles, exact RVFI sources/results, wrong-path suppression and contiguous retirement order.'''},\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Selected-angle hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
