 json\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/b57a151a/d31a4914/branch_probe')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing_flags',options=(0,1,2))\n(p/'timing_flags_result.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(summarize(r),indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"placement_failed\": false,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 77.137,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    78.69,\n    77.137,\n    77.137\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      78.69,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      77.137,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      77.137,\n      15\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lut4\": 3669,\n  \"ff\": 1690,\n  \"lutram\": 0,\n  \"bsram\": 4,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"logic_levels\": 15,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.wb_result_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_illegal_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.708,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 18.002,\n    \"logic_cells\": 40,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r11s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261005-002-r11s1\ntitle: \\\"Select narrow branch relation flags after comparing bypass candidates\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 199.86 iter/sec at 90.490 MHz and 4,527,646\n  marker-bounded cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Structural r9s1 added\n  dependency latency and lost fitness despite 103.173 MHz; r10s1 added\n  result banks and forwarding fanout and fell to 77.992 MHz. The recorded\n  champion critical path traverses forwarded operands, EX branch recovery\n  and ID control. This proposal isolates that control path without adding\n  stages, changing the ALU or changing instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the branch comparator after the two 32-bit forwarding muxes with\n  a small relation matrix over the existing registered operand candidates.\n  Evaluate equality, unsigned-less and signed-less before choosing the\n  forwarding sources, select only these three relation bits, and decode\n  branch_op once afterward. This is one structural relocation of branch\n  operand arbitration across comparison. Keep the ordinary ALU, shifter,\n  address generation, divider and all architectural operand muxes unchanged.\n\n  Let A[0]=in.rs1_val, A[1]=fwd_ex_mem, A[2]=fwd_mem_wb;\n  let B[0]=in.rs2_val, B[1]=fwd_ex_mem, B[2]=fwd_mem_wb.\n  The existing qualified fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel choose one candidate\n  each. For a source selector, derive three local one-hot enables for saved,\n  early and WB sources, preserving the existing default-to-saved behavior.\n  Do not introduce additional producer sources, bank kinds or qualification\n  into forward_unit. Candidate evaluation has no side effects.\n\n  For each distinct candidate pair compute eq=(A==B) and ltu=(A<B).\n  Compute signed-less by sharing the unsigned comparison:\n  lts=(A[31] \"'^ B[31]) ? A[31] : ltu.\n  Represent each pair'\"'s flags as {lts,ltu,eq}. Avoid a separate signed\n  subtract/compare tree. Only six independent pairs are needed:\n  (A0,B0), (A0,early), (A0,WB), (early,B0), (WB,B0), and (early,WB).\n  The early/early and WB/WB diagonal pairs are always {0,0,1}.\n  Derive the reversed WB/early pair from early/WB flags:\n  eq_rev=eq; ltu_rev=\"'!ltu && !eq; lts_rev=!lts && !eq.\n  These identities apply to both signed and unsigned total ordering.\n  Preserve all 32 operand bits; do not truncate comparisons or assume\n  sign bits agree because register numbers or destination matches agree.\n\n  Select the three-bit relation result with a balanced masked-OR tree,\n  first across the three rs2 candidates and then across the three rs1\n  candidates. Branch operation decode appears only AFTER flag selection:\n  BEQ=eq, BNE=!eq, BLT=lts, BGE=!lts, BLTU=ltu, BGEU=!ltu;\n  reserved branch operations produce false as today. Do not distribute\n  branch_op decoding to each candidate comparator. Do not replace this\n  with nine copies of a complete operation-dependent predicate or ALU.\n  The selected relation is exactly the relation of the same architectural\n  rs1/rs2 that the existing forwarding muxes choose.\n\n  Use this result for the existing branch_cond, then preserve the current\n  branch_taken, valid qualification, target calculation, alignment checks,\n  redirect-over-stall priority and ID squash controls. Keep EX branch\n  resolution in its current cycle; no predictor, early decode redirect,\n  registered delayed recovery or extra branch bubble is added. Unselected\n  candidate relations cannot cause a trap or redirect. JAL/JALR behavior,\n  link values, target addresses and fault suppression remain unchanged.\n\n  Retain the original selected full-width rs1 and rs2 for the ALU, store\n  data, LSU/JALR address calculation, real divider requests, EX/MEM source\n  snapshots, MEM multiplier operands and RVFI. Preserve ID-aligned raw\n  forwarding-match capture, EX/MEM-over-WB priority, x0 treatment, current\n  producer write eligibility and retained MEM/WB forwarding during stalls.\n  Branch comparisons must remain correct when a source comes from a held\n  WB producer whose retirement valid was cleared; use the authoritative\n  existing selectors rather than adding new valid gates. Use the same\n  relation topology in real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds, preserving\n  every exact M-extension substitute and real arithmetic unit.\n\n  Private probes in this research turn provide negative evidence for\n  broader versions: nine complete ALU lanes reached only 66.049 MHz;\n  a transparent fetch buffer saved 3.668 percent cycles and passed all\n  53 unchanged formal checks but reached only 85.553 MHz median; nine\n  complete operation-dependent branch predicates reached 79.730 MHz.\n  None is proposed or evidence of a fitness improvement. The final\n  relation-only version specifically removes replicated branch-op\n  selection, shares signed/unsigned comparison, uses constant diagonals\n  and shares the reversed producer pair to reduce replication and fanout.\n  Its timing and correctness results must be recorded before treating\n  the forecast as measured; an ongoing private probe is only preliminary.\n\n  Forecast an unmeasured eight percent fitness gain with low confidence.\n  At the unchanged champion cycle count, acceptance above 209.05356\n  iter/sec requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 94.653 MHz.\n  The intended benefit is removing forwarding selection from the inputs\n  of branch reduction/carry chains while selecting only three bits after\n  comparison. The competing shift path, flag selection latency, additional\n  operand fanout and placement are the main risks; the unsuccessful broader\n  predicate matrix makes this a deliberately low-confidence hypothesis.\n  Require three-option vendor timing, unchanged formal gates, retirement\n  cosim and canonical marker-bounded CoreMark validation. Preserve nret=1,\n  all ports and all hard invariants; change no evaluator file or check.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_relations.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a combinational branch relation unit over saved, EX/MEM and WB\n      candidate words. Compute six equality/unsigned-less pairs, derive\n      signed-less from signs and unsigned-less, use constant producer\n      diagonals and exact reverse-pair identities. Select three-bit flags\n      after comparison using existing forwarding selectors and decode the\n      six branch operations only once after selection. No arithmetic\n      instruction, pipeline state, register write or memory side effect\n      is introduced by this module.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Instantiate the relation unit with the raw registered source candidates\n      and existing selectors; replace only branch_cond computation. Retain\n      both full-width architectural operand muxes and all ALU, shift, LSU,\n      JALR, divider, source snapshot, EX/MEM, trap and redirect behavior.\n      Avoid additional branch_op qualification ahead of the relation unit.\n  - file: test/test_branch_relations.py\n    description: |\n      Compare all nine selector pairs and six branch predicates against exact\n      scalar signed/unsigned relations, emphasizing equality, reverse pairs,\n      sign boundaries, INT_MIN/MAX, zero/all-ones and independent random\n      words. Verify both constant diagonals, selector default behavior and\n      invariance to unselected source changes. Check reserved branch ops\n      retain their existing false condition.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Include the relation-unit source and retain every existing execute\n      assertion. Cover selected forwarded branch operands, aligned and\n      misaligned taken targets, not-taken conditions and downstream holds,\n      checking redirect/trap and recorded architectural source values.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Include the new RTL source and retain all architectural and schedule\n      assertions. Add branches sourcing every saved/EX/WB combination,\n      youngest writers to the same register, x0, load/MUL/DIV producers and\n      retained WB values during long memory holds. Check all six predicates,\n      exact source fields, successor PCs, contiguous orders and wrong-path\n      side-effect suppression with both buses stalled, without new bubbles.\n'\"''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nx=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()); jsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Validated final relation hypothesis',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
