ponse to pass directly to ID on the same cycle. If ID cannot accept\n  it, capture it in the queue instead. With queued data, ID always sees\n  the oldest entry, independently of the CURRENT io_imemReady signal.\n  Support simultaneous dequeue and enqueue, including a full queue t\n…[5876 of 8948 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:81bd9b29bbebe0b0]…\nng, registered recovery and nret=1 RVFI unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_fetch_queue.py\n    description: |\n      Verify empty bypass, capture on consumer hold, occupancy bounds,\n      full simultaneous push/pop, wraparound, stable oldest head and exact\n      once/in-order delivery. Exercise unavailable responses, reset and\n      recovery coincident with each enqueue/dequeue combination; check\n      captured PCs and prediction bits with a queue reference model.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise fetch-ahead during late-result hazards, divider waits and\n      long dmem holds with independently varying imemReady. Cover queued\n      branches/jumps, correct predictions, recovery with full queue,\n      changing predictor state, wrong-path stores/DIV and illegal targets.\n      Check exact RVFI operands/results/successors/orders, stable memory\n      handshakes, one retirement per instruction, no wrong-path effects,\n      continuous-ready throughput and forward progress. Retain all tests.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
