{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The previous registered multiplier added three cycles per MUL and lost fitness. I’ll instead use the existing MEM stage for multiplication: capture forwarded operands in EX, compute the product in MEM, and stall only an immediately dependent instruction. This removes forwarding muxes from the multiplier’s clock path while allowing independent instructions to proceed."}}
