{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"tail -4 cores/bench/generated/hypgen-late-mul/pipeline.log; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r5s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=16\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('Forecast a 12 percent fitness gain with medium confidence, from higher', 'Forecast a 16 percent fitness gain with medium confidence, from higher')\nh=h.replace('These are forecasts, not measurements.', '''An isolated prototype of this exact retiming measured Gowin placement\noptions 0/1/2 at 65.713/70.072/70.072 MHz, median 70.072 MHz, versus\n60.076 MHz for the champion. Its canonical 2K/-O3/10-iteration CoreMark\nrun with both bus stalls took 4,527,646 marked cycles, only 0.80 percent\nmore than the champion, and passed the unmodified validator for all\nfive CRCs, the success literal, timing markers and no OOB accesses.\nThe measured product is 154.76475 iter/sec, 15.71 percent above 133.75\nand above the 139.9025 acceptance threshold. Placement option 0 used\n3352 LUTs and 1657 registers, versus 3303 and 1613 currently, and two\nDSPs. Its worst reported path was 20.512 ns, 13 cells; the multiplier\nno longer appeared on that worst path.\n\nAll 53 generated checks from the unchanged single-channel formal config\npassed with ALTOPS in a private staging tree; real and ALTOPS multiplier\nvector suites passed; selftest retirement cosim passed both zero-wait\nand with both stalls. All 27 prototype pipeline tests passed, including\nadded MUL-to-DIV, retained WB product under a long store stall, JALR,\nyounger-writer priority and x0 checks. Existing selectors/cycle-gap\nassertions tied to immediate EX multiplication were changed to assert\nthe specific intended WB source and single dependency bubble, retaining\nall operand, arithmetic, retirement, trap and memory checks. These\nprototype results substantiate the rounded 16 percent forecast; the\norchestrator must still reproduce the implementation and run every\nnormal correctness and fitness gate.''')\nh=h.replace('Generalize the existing readiness-qualified load-use detector to cover\\\\na valid legal multiply in ID/EX.', '''Generalize the existing readiness-qualified load-use detector to cover\na valid legal multiply in ID/EX. The prototype changes only core wiring:\nfeed id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read OR id_ex_mul to the hazard unit's existing\nid_ex_mem_read input; no hazard_unit port or algorithm change is needed.''')\nh=h.replace('Exclude multiply producers from EX/MEM forwarding:\\\\ntheir result is not ready there.', '''Exclude multiply producers from EX/MEM forwarding by driving the\nexisting forward_unit ex_mem_w_en with ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write AND NOT\nex_mem_mul; do not change its registered matching or qualify held WB\nforwarding by MEM/WB.valid. No EX-stage edit is needed: normal_payload\nalready captures forwarded rs1_val and rs2_val. Their result is not\nready in EX/MEM.''')\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['changes']=[x for x in d['changes'] if x['file'] not in ('rtl/ex_stage.sv','rtl/hazard_unit.sv')]\nfor x in d['changes']:\n if x['file']=='rtl/core.sv':\n  x['description']='''Define id_ex_mul as ID/EX valid AND NOT is_illegal AND alu_op in\nMUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU. Feed ctrl.mem_read OR id_ex_mul to the existing\nhazard input id_ex_mem_read. Define ex_mem_mul from the same four\nregistered op equalities and gate the existing forward_unit\nex_mem_w_en with ctrl.reg_write AND NOT ex_mem_mul. Preserve the\nunchanged hazard algorithm, forward-unit registered-match alignment,\nMEM/WB forwarding eligibility during holds, all ports, nret=1 and RVFI.\n'''\n if x['file']=='test/test_pipeline.py':\n  x['description']+='''Update only old EX-multiply selector and no-bubble timing assertions\nto check the intended WB forwarding and exact one-bubble dependent\nschedule; retain all architectural results and invariant assertions.\nExplicitly assert consecutive independent MULs still retire each cycle.\n'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=78))\nprint('Revised expected gain:',d['expected_impact'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
