{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r7s1.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-002-r7s1',\n 'title':'Split fixed immediate shifts from a registered late barrel-shift lane',\n 'category':'structural',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 173.20 iter/sec at 78.418 MHz with 4,527,646 marked\nCoreMark cycles. Its worst path starts at a registered forwarding match\nand crosses EX operand selection and the ALU before reaching data memory.\nThe successful r6s1 structural change moved multiplication behind a\nregistered operand boundary while retaining early ordinary-ALU forwarding\nand unified registered WB completion. The remaining five-level barrel\nshifter is a promising next execution unit to isolate. LESSONS.md is absent;\nall six prior structural attempts were examined, and none split shift\nexecution. Blocking execution and uniformly delayed redirects previously\nlost enough cycles to cancel their clock gains.\n\nA reference-ISS replay of the canonical marked workload found 274,453\nshifts, all immediate forms. Shifts by one or two account for 117,700 of\nthese and 42,660 adjacent raw-source dependencies. Their computation can\nuse fixed bit wiring and a small one-versus-two mux, avoiding the general\nfive-bit shift network. Preserving that early path limits the cycle cost\nof moving the general barrel shifter into MEM.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Split shift execution into an early fixed-immediate path and a registered\nlate barrel-shift completion lane. This is one structural change to the\nshift execution boundary: SLLI/SRLI/SRAI with amounts exactly 1 or 2 remain\nsingle-cycle EX results; every other immediate shift and every register\nSLL/SRL/SRA becomes a late MEM result. Preserve the stage count, single\nissue, EX branch resolution, nret=1, and the current retirement boundary.\nDo not add a blocking shift state machine or general MEM-to-EX shift bypass.\n\nIn ID, register two payload bits alongside the normal operands:\nshift_early = dec_alu_src && (dec_alu_op is SLL/SRL/SRA) &&\n              (instruction[24:20] equals 1 or 2);\nshift_two = (instruction[24:20] equals 2).\nUse the validated decoder outputs, so register forms, illegal encodings\nand all non-shift instructions cannot acquire early shift eligibility.\nReset and hold these bits with the ID/EX payload, independently of flush;\nthe existing separate controls and valid bit keep bubbles inert. No\nforwarded value, redirect or imem-ready signal enters this classification.\n\nIn EX, implement only the early fixed shifts with concatenations:\nleft-by-one {rs1[30:0],1'b0}; left-by-two {rs1[29:0],2'b0};\nright-by-one {fill,rs1[31:1]}; right-by-two {{2{fill}},rs1[31:2]}.\nHere rs1 is the fully forwarded operand and fill is rs1[31] only for SRA,\notherwise zero. shift_two selects the fixed amount; the already registered\nalu_op selects left versus right and logical versus arithmetic fill.\nSelect this result when shift_early is set, ahead of the existing jump-link\nand ordinary ALU result selection. There must be no variable-shift operator\non this early path. Set an elaboration-time ENABLE_SHIFTS parameter on alu\n(default true for its existing standalone suite) to false in EX, returning\nzero for its three shift cases there. Keep all other ALU operations and\nexact M-extension ALTOPS constants unchanged. The synthesized EX instance\nmust contain no general barrel shifter.\n\nAdd shift_late and five-bit shift_amount to EX/MEM. Capture shift_amount\nfrom alu_b[4:0], which already correctly chooses immediate versus forwarded\nrs2. Capture shift_late as a shift-operation match AND NOT shift_early.\nReuse the existing captured fully forwarded rs1_val as the MEM shifter data;\npreserve rs2_val separately as the architectural RVFI source value even for\nimmediate shifts. Hold this metadata with the existing downstream dmem\nfreeze. Normal bubbles clear controls/readiness and are side-effect-free.\n\nInstantiate a small combinational shifter in MEM from registered rs1_val,\nshift_amount and alu_op, with exact SLL/SRL/signed-SRA semantics for amounts\n0 through 31. Qualify shift completion with in.valid, \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal,\nand in.shift_late. Select the completed shift before the unified WB register:\nin.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : is_mul ? mul_result :\nis_shift ? shift_result : in.alu_result.\nEarly fixed shifts follow the ordinary in.alu_result path. WB still drives\nregistered wb_result directly, without a post-register completion mux.\nThe general barrel shifter and forwarding operand mux therefore occupy\ndifferent clock paths.\n\nRegister fwd_ready false for late shifts as well as existing loads and\nmultiplies; retain readiness for early fixed shifts. Concretely extend the\nexisting EX expression with NOT(!in.shift_early && shift_op_match), preserving\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write, load/multiply exclusion and divider completion.\nExtend the existing valid-legal late-producer interlock in core with\nid_ex_shift = id_ex_w.valid && !id_ex_w.ctrl.is_illegal &&\n              !id_ex_w.shift_early && shift_op_match.\nFeed mem_read OR id_ex_mul OR id_ex_shift to the existing hazard input.\nKeep readiness-qualified raw source comparisons, x0 exclusion and all\nhazard priorities unchanged. A immediately dependent late-shift consumer\ngets exactly one bubble and receives the result from registered WB;\nearly shifts retain EX/MEM forwarding with no new bubble. Independent\ninstructions and consecutive independent late shifts still issue every\nclock. Do not decode shift readiness from MEM combinationally.\n\nPreserve youngest-writer priority, registered dependency alignment,\nwrite-first register reads, and MEM/WB data retention during dmem holds.\nWB forwarding remains usable after valid clears; register writes remain\nvalid-qualified. A shift blocked behind older memory advances exactly\nonce, and its completion retires once. Shift-to-store, branch, JALR,\nMUL and DIV dependencies must use correct forwarded architectural values.\nDivider requests still snapshot operands before older sources drain.\nWrong-path operations never reach side effects. Retain all decoder,\nalignment-trap, memory-order, reset, RVFI-source and contiguous-order rules.\nUse this identical early/late shift schedule under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS:\nonly M-extension arithmetic receives its existing substitutes.\n\nAn isolated prototype of exactly the specified amounts and boundaries\nmeasured Gowin placement options 0/1/2 at 83.566/85.865/85.865 MHz, median\n85.865 MHz, versus the champion'\"'s 78.418 MHz. Option 0 used 3368 LUTs,\n1640 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its worst path was 17.261 ns,\nversus the recorded champion's 18.433 ns. The canonical 2K/-O3/ten-iteration\nCoreMark simulation with both approximately 22 percent bus stalls took\n4,611,078 marker-bounded cycles, 1.843 percent more than the champion.\nThe unchanged UART validator accepted all five canonical CRCs and the\nsuccess literal; the run reached EBREAK, had both markers and no OOB.\nThe measured product is 186.21459 iter/sec, 7.514 percent above 173.20\nand above the required 181.1672 acceptance threshold. Existing pipeline\nand EX integration runner checks passed with the packed-field/source-list\nupdates; targeted shift and formal validation must also pass.\n\nForecast a rounded 8 percent fitness gain with medium confidence. These\nare isolated prototype measurements, not a substitute for the orchestrator's\nimplementation, full correctness gates or fitness evaluation. At the\nmeasured cycle count acceptance requires median Fmax above 83.53761 MHz,\ngiving about 2.33 MHz of margin. The principal risk is another ALU,\nredirect or MEM product-selection path limiting timing after replication,\nor an implementation changing the early-shift eligibility and cycle cost.\nPreserve every evaluator file and every hard invariant, including nret=1\nports, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, canonical CRC/UART checks and markers.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/shifter.sv','description':'''Add the combinational general SLL/SRL/SRA completion module using a\n32-bit operand and five-bit amount, with complete assignments and exact\nsigned arithmetic-right semantics. The core uses it only from registered\nEX/MEM operands in MEM; no shift-result bypass feeds EX.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add shift_early and shift_two to the ID/EX payload after imm; add\nshift_late and five-bit shift_amount to EX/MEM after alu_result. Preserve\nall architectural source fields, unified WB result and retirement width.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture the validated immediate-shift-by-1-or-2 eligibility and fixed\namount bit with ordinary ID/EX payload reset/hold logic. Preserve raw\nregister addressing and the separate flush/valid/control behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add a default-enabled elaboration-time ENABLE_SHIFTS parameter. When\nfalse, the SLL/SRL/SRA cases return zero and instantiate no barrel\nshifter. Preserve the default standalone ALU interface/results, every\nother operation and all exact existing M-extension ALTOPS expressions.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Disable the ALU barrel shifter and implement only fixed 1/2-bit early\nimmediate shifts with concatenations. Capture late-shift flag and exact\nalu_b amount; register early readiness for fixed shifts and exclude\nlate shifts. Preserve forwarded RVFI sources, trap/link/redirect behavior,\ndmem holds, divider metadata and cleared side-effect controls in bubbles.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Instantiate the general shifter on captured rs1_val/amount/op and\nselect its result only for valid legal late shifts before wb_result.\nEarly shifts retain ordinary ALU completion. Preserve multiplier/load\ncompletion, external memory request logic and retained WB data on holds.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Add valid-legal non-early shifts to the existing load/multiply-use\nhazard input. Preserve the registered forwarding topology and hazard\nunit algorithm, all memory ports and nret=1 channel-0 RVFI retirement.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_shifter.py','description':'''Verify all amounts 0 through 31 and exact SLL/SRL/SRA bit results with\nzero/all-one operands, single-bit patterns, negative arithmetic shifts\nand seeded random vectors. Preserve standalone ALU shift assertions.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Update packed ID/EX and EX/MEM field lists, preserving all existing\nassertions. Check fixed early wiring for both amounts and every shift\nmode, late amount capture for immediate/register forms, readiness,\nforwarded source metadata and downstream holds.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add shifter.sv to the source list. Cover all six shift instructions\nand all amounts; assert zero new bubble for immediate amounts 1/2,\nexactly one bubble for dependent late shifts and consecutive retirement\nof independent late shifts. Check WB forwarding to ALU/store/branch/\nJALR/MUL/DIV, x0 and younger-writer priority, both bus stalls, long WB\nretention and wrong-path suppression. Retain every existing arithmetic,\ntrap, order, memory and decoder assertion and the ALTOPS scheduling check.\n'''}\n ]}\n# Keep block scalars for reviewable long descriptions.\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef string(d,s):return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nD.add_representer(str,string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nprint('Total counted shift instructions:',274453,'early:',117700)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
