t blocked behind older memory advances exactly\nonce, and its completion retires once. Shift-to-store, branch, JALR,\nMUL and DIV dependencies must use correct forwarded architectural values.\nDivider requests still snapshot operands before older sources drain.\nWrong-path operations never reach side effects. Retain all decoder,\nalignment-trap, memory-order, reset, RVFI-source and contiguous-order rules.\nUse this identical early/late shift schedule under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS:\nonly M-extension arithmetic receives its existing substitutes.\n\nAn isolated prototype of exactly the specified amounts and boundaries\nmeasured Gowin placement options 0/1/2 at 83.566/85.865/85.865 MHz, median\n85.865 MHz, versus the champion'\"'s 78.418 MHz. Option 0 used 3368 LUTs,\n1640 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its worst path was 17.261 ns,\nversus the recorded champion's 18.433 ns. The canonical 2K/-O3/ten-iteration\nCoreMark simulation with both approximately 22 percent bus stalls took\n4,611,078 marker-bounded cycles, 1.843 percent more than the champion.\nThe unchanged UART validator accepted all five canonical CRCs and the\nsuccess literal; the run reached EBREAK, had both markers and no OOB.\nThe measured product is 186.21459 iter/sec, 7.514 percent above 173.20\nand above the required 181.1672 acceptance threshold. Existing pipeline\nand EX integration runner checks passed with the packed-field/source-list\nupdates; targeted shift and formal validation must also pass.\n\nForecast a rounded 8 percent fitness gain with medium confidence. These\nare isolated prototype measurements, not a substitute for the orchestrator's\nimplementation, full correctness gates or fitness evaluation. At the\nmeasured cycle count acceptance requires median Fmax above 83.53761 MHz,\ngiving about 2.33 MHz of margin. The principal risk is another ALU,\nredirect or MEM product-selection path limiting timing after replication,\nor an implementation changing the early-shift eligibility and cycle cost.\nPreserve every evaluator file and every hard invariant, including nret=1\nports, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, canonical CRC/UART checks and markers.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/shifter.sv','description':'''Add the combinational general SLL/SRL/SRA completion module using a\n32-bit operand and five-bit amount, with complete assignments and exact\nsigned arithmetic-right semantics. The core uses it only from registered\nEX/MEM operands in MEM; no shift-result bypass feeds EX.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add shift_early and shift_two to the ID/EX payload after imm; add\nshift_late and five-bit shift_amount to EX/MEM after alu_result. Preserve\nall architectural source fields, unified WB result and retirement width.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture the validated immediate-shift-by-1-or-2 eligibility and fixed\namount bit with ordinary ID/EX payload reset/hold logic. Preserve raw\nregister addressing and the separate flush/valid/control behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add a default-enabled elaboration-time ENABLE_SHIFTS parameter. When\nfalse, the SLL/SRL/SRA cases return zero and instantiate no barrel\nshifter. Preserve the default standalone ALU interface/results, every\nother operation and all exact existing M-extension ALTOPS expressions.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Disable the ALU barrel shifter and implement only fixed 1/2-bit early\nimmediate shifts with concatenations. Capture late-shift flag and exact\nalu_b amount; register early readiness for fixed shifts and exclude\nlate shifts. Preserve forwarded RVFI sources, trap/link/redirect behavior,\ndmem holds, divider metadata and cleared side-effect controls in bubbles.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Instantiate the general shifter on captured rs1_val/amount/op and\nselect its result only for valid legal late shifts