nder.\nPerform one unsigned divide iteration per clock for 32 iterations, with\nregistered operand normalization and result sign correction. Keep all\nother integer operations, including multiplication, on their existing\nexecution path. This is one structural change: isolate variable-latency\ndivision from the fast single-cycle ALU, rather than redesign the pipeline.\n\nOn a valid divide instruction, accept exactly one request when the older\nMEM instruction is not blocking EX. Capture the fully forwarded rs1/rs2,\noperation and instruction metadata before older forwarding sources drain.\nHold the fetch PC and ID/EX instruction until the result can advance;\nallow older MEM/WB instructions to drain exactly once. While division is\nrunning, inject invalid E\n…[39904 of 42976 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:55518358c6ec5819]…\n 8 percent fitness gain with medium confidence. These\nare isolated prototype measurements, not a substitute for the orchestrator's\nimplementation, full correctness gates or fitness evaluation. At the\nmeasured cycle count acceptance requires median Fmax above 83.53761 MHz,\ngiving about 2.33 MHz of margin. The principal risk is another ALU,\nredirect or MEM product-selection path limiting timing after replication,\nor an implementation changing the early-shift eligibility and cycle cost.\nPreserve every evaluator file and every hard invariant, including nret=1\nports, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, canonical CRC/UART checks and markers.\n\n  notes: \nhyp-20261005-003-r7s2 predictor Compact micro-BTB with registered training and live successor checks\n  outcome: regression fitness: 181.49 Fmax: 77.152 cycles: 4251084 path: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.wb_result_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -7.952, 'arrival_ns': 18.246, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
