successive stages.\n\nGeneralize the existing readiness-qualified load-use detector to cover a\nvalid legal multiply in ID/EX. The prototype changes only core wiring: feed\nid_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read OR id_ex_mul to the hazard unit's existing\nid_ex_mem_read input; no hazard_unit port or algorithm change is needed. If\nthe next accepted instruction names its nonzero destination, hold the fetch\nPC and insert one ID/EX control bubble, exactly as for a load. Conservative\nraw source comparisons are acceptable initially. Exclude multiply producers\nfrom EX/MEM forwarding by driving the existing forward_unit ex_mem_w_en with\ne\n…[23733 of 26805 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2961593bf5637929]…\nhitectural results, RVFI values and\nordering assertions. All five existing execute integration cases and a\nnew invalid-control case passed, covering stale ALU/load/store/branch/\nJAL/JALR/MUL/DIV payloads with no effect. These probe results do not replace the\nimplementation phase's required correctness and fitness gates.\n\nForecast a rounded 6 percent fitness gain with low confidence because\nthe measured clock margin over acceptance is only 1.0004 MHz, or\n1.146 percent. Both removing decode squashes and removing match squashes\nare essential: retaining the match-register flush measured only\n86.705 MHz median and missed acceptance. Keep this precise topology\nrather than adding broader validity gating to the forwarding network\nor changing the arithmetic, branch comparator or instruction schedule.\n\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.wb_result_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_25_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.588, 'arrival_ns': 16.882, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
