ion counter per entry. A matching unconditional entry predicts\nits last resolved target; a conditional entry predicts its target only\nwhen the counter MSB is set. Misses predict PC+4. Initialize a newly\nallocated conditional entry weakly toward its resolved outcome. Train\nboth branch outcomes, learn JAL/JALR targets, and refresh indirect\ntargets on resolution. Do not add a return stack or global history.\n\nLookup uses only the registered fetch PC, not an instruction-memory\ndecode or a forwarding-dependent operand. Store full targets rather\nthan adding branch immediates on the fetch critical path. Reset entry\nvalid bits, and keep invalid payloads unobservable; avoid resetting the\ntag/target arrays so the vendor can infer distributed storage. Keep the\npredictor small enough that its lookup and PC mux remain we\n…[55506 of 58578 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:585f05106bf94646]…\n Accepted recovery overrides imem\nstalls and load-use holds; a correct prediction admits the ready target\nfetch without squashing it. Preserve existing hazard/forwarding rules,\nMEM/WB producer retention during dmem stalls, divider request/result\nhandshakes, effective-address bypass and MEM multiplication. Do not\nintroduce predictor state into divider metadata or alter arithmetic.\n\nThe hypothesis is that loop-biased static prediction removes enough\ndirect-transfer bubbles while retaining substantially more of the\nchampion's Fmax than dynamic table predictors. Measure canonical\nCoreMark cycles and median Gowin Fmax together; lower cycles alone do\nnot establish improvement. Keep nret=1, all external ports, decoder\nlegality, exact RVFI successors/orders, and every existing correctness,\nCRC, UART, MMIO-marker and memory-bound check unchanged.\n\nNOTES \n\nID hyp-20261005-003-r10s2 TITLE (slot 2 hypothesis-gen failed) OUTCOME broken FITNESS None DELTA None FMAX None CYCLES None\nPATH None\nMOTIVATION \nHYPOTHESIS \nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "compl