{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The static predictor reduced CoreMark cycles by about 6%, but its lower Fmax kept the gain below the acceptance threshold. Target-table predictors also lost clock speed. I’m focusing on a small direction predictor that computes direct targets from the fetched instruction and keeps recovery logic shallow.\n"}}
