{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r11s2.yaml')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('Add one 32-entry agree direction predictor','Add one 16-entry agree direction predictor')\ns=s.replace('Index with fetch PC[6:2].','Index with fetch PC[5:2] XOR PC[10:7], a four-bit folded PC index.')\ns=s.replace('containing a five-bit index, one agreement bit and one valid bit.','containing a four-bit folded index, one agreement bit and one valid bit.')\ns=s.replace('Add 32 independent two-bit saturating agreement counters initialized\\\\n      strongly agree, PC[6:2] lookup with balanced MSB selection, static','Add 16 independent two-bit saturating agreement counters initialized\\\\n      strongly agree, folded PC[5:2] XOR PC[10:7] lookup with balanced MSB selection, static')\ns=s.replace('  Implement counters as independent', '  Implement counters as independent')\ns=s.replace('  Preselect a conditional repair target from the carried prediction:', '''  Flatten the predictor's PC successor selection into mutually exclusive\n  masked terms combined by a balanced OR: hold PC, accepted PC+4,\n  accepted predicted B target, accepted predicted J target, or repair\n  target. Repair masks all ordinary terms; stalls select hold unless\n  an accepted repair overrides them. Register this complete next-PC\n  each clock with reset priority. Avoid a serial B/J mux followed by\n  taken/fall-through, repair, and late PC clock-enable selection. This\n  is the timing-sensitive integration of this direction predictor, with\n  unchanged acceptance and recovery semantics.\n\n  Preselect a conditional repair target from the carried prediction:''')\ns=s.replace('  This forecast is unmeasured.', '''  This forecast is not a measured final fitness. A reference replay of\n  the canonical marked region validated all five CRCs and the success\n  literal without OOB accesses: 529588 conditional branches, 294425\n  taken, 49367 JAL and 13735 JALR. Static opcode bias missed 69808\n  conditionals; the sixteen-entry folded agree table missed 46312.\n  A thirty-two-entry agree table with folded contiguous five-bit fields\n  missed 43029, only 3283 fewer with twice the counter state. Select\n  sixteen entries. These are software replay statistics with immediate\n  training, not cycle-accurate evidence.\n\n  An isolated first RTL probe with delayed training completed canonical\n  CoreMark with both bus stalls in 4229842 marked cycles and passed the\n  unchanged CRC/UART validator with no OOB. Its serial PC selection\n  reached only 82.428 MHz median across Gowin options 0/1/2, so it would\n  fail acceptance. Its worst path ended at the fetch PC clock enable.\n  The proposed parallel masked PC selection addresses that observed\n  predictor integration bottleneck. At 4229842 cycles the final design\n  needs median Fmax above 88.426353 MHz. Do not claim the initial probe\n  as a successful candidate or use its cycle count to waive timing.''')\ns=s.replace('      direct targets with parallel split-carry addition. Emit selected','      direct targets with parallel split-carry addition. Use mutually\\\\n      exclusive masked PC hold/sequential/B/J/repair terms and balanced OR\\\\n      selection instead of nested successor muxes and a late PC enable. Emit selected')\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined sixteen-entry hypothesis remains schema-valid')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
