n-direct instructions select PC+4. Store no\ntags, target entries, counters, validity arrays or training metadata.\n\nCarry only the actual selected predicted_taken bit through if_id_t\nand id_ex_t. Keep prediction decode and all wide payloads independent\nof redirect, flush and fetch validity. Capture this bit with the\nordinary instruction payload, holding it through true pipeline holds.\nAdvance fetch PC to the selected successor precisely when that same\ninstruction enters ID/EX as valid; imem stalls, load/multiply-use\nbubbles, older dmem freezes and divider waits consume no prediction.\n\nUse exact split-carry B/J target generation to bound fetch dela\n…[1464 of 4536 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ae2e8ba1ab1acc39]…\ned recovery overrides imem\nstalls and load-use holds; a correct prediction admits the ready target\nfetch without squashing it. Preserve existing hazard/forwarding rules,\nMEM/WB producer retention during dmem stalls, divider request/result\nhandshakes, effective-address bypass and MEM multiplication. Do not\nintroduce predictor state into divider metadata or alter arithmetic.\n\nThe hypothesis is that loop-biased static prediction removes enough\ndirect-transfer bubbles while retaining substantially more of the\nchampion's Fmax than dynamic table predictors. Measure canonical\nCoreMark cycles and median Gowin Fmax together; lower cycles alone do\nnot establish improvement. Keep nret=1, all external ports, decoder\nlegality, exact RVFI successors/orders, and every existing correctness,\nCRC, UART, MMIO-marker and memory-bound check unchanged.\n\n{'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 205.42, 'cycles': 4253728, 'fmax_mhz': 87.379}\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 6, in <module>\nKeyError: 'hypothesis'\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
