{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_23", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Resolve agree-prediction from registered full branch operands in MEM',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. Predictor history was reviewed: broad target tables\nand repeated recovery retiming regressed, while the sixteen-counter agree\npredictor succeeded. The champion already applies recovery in MEM and\nscores 224.09 iter/sec at 98.964 MHz with 4416239 marked cycles. Round\n13 registered byte-comparison results but still compared forwarded EX\noperands before those registers; it regressed to 95.096 MHz. The next\nspecific predictor angle is to remove the entire conditional comparison\nfrom the forwarding network, using the existing EX/MEM source registers.\nA canonical reference replay found 13735 returns and 46315 immediate-update\nagree misses in the measured region. Their limited cycle headroom makes\npredictor-validation timing a stronger candidate than adding a return\nstack or a larger direction table.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing sixteen-entry agree direction policy, folded PC index,\ninstruction bias, exact direct B/J target generation and MEM recovery\nschedule. Move the ENTIRE conditional branch comparison to MEM, starting\nfrom the existing registered EX/MEM forwarded rs1_val/rs2_val. EX must\ncontain no conditional equality or ordering comparator, completed branch\ndirection, conditional mismatch, or conditional target-fault logic feeding\nits timed controls. This differs from r13s2's partial comparator split:\nEX now only captures the forwarded architectural source words, target,\nand register-only prediction metadata; all operand relations begin after\nthat register. Reduce fanout on the forwarding outputs feeding the\nchampion's WB-to-EX arithmetic critical path without changing arithmetic.\n\nCapture a compact conditional event eligibility, static bias, and early\nrecovery polarity (branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken) alongside EX/MEM.\nEligibility requires a valid legal conditional instruction, aligned direct\ntarget, actual EX advancement, no unfinished divide and no older squash.\nHold it on precisely the downstream EX/MEM stall; bubbles and squashed\nyounger branches clear eligibility only. Keep this metadata independent\nof divider snapshots. Use the already captured source words, branch_op,\nPC and branch target, rather than adding another pair of source registers.\n\nIn MEM compare four eight-bit equality/less-than lanes from those source\nflops, flip only the registered sign bits for signed ordering, and finish\nwith a balanced significance merge. Actual condition is branch_base XOR\nbranch_op[0]; mismatch is branch_base XOR the early captured recovery\npolarity. Branch operation and both comparator operands must refer to the\nsame owning MEM instruction. The conditional repair target remains the\nexisting EX/MEM-registered target preselected in EX by predicted_taken:\nPC+4 for a predicted-taken branch and PC+imm otherwise. Keep JAL/JALR's\ncurrent registered recovery eligibility and target. Conditional MEM\nmismatch drives the existing redirect in the SAME cycle that champion\nrecovery_valid_q does; do not add a register or an EX recovery bypass.\n\nThe branch's complete architectural successor and taken-misaligned-target\ntrap finish at MEM/WB using the same MEM predicate. Preserve default-illegal\ndecoding through EX; only a legal taken branch with a misaligned target\nadds the branch fault and reports PC+4. A conditional branch never writes\nregisters or memory, so this deferred branch fault must not be routed back\nthrough EX ctrl/fwd_ready or through timed MEM arithmetic enables. Keep\nall JAL/JALR alignment, suppressed-link behavior, memory alignment and\nnon-branch writeback semantics unchanged. Any provisional EX conditional\npc_next/branch_taken is internal; retirement always reports the complete\nresolved successor and trap. Prefer one shared MEM predicate; a separate\nverification-only completion expression may exist only if synthesis\nprunes it and it cannot recreate an EX comparator or timed fault path.\n\nGenerate predictor_train_t combinationally from the owning MEM record:\nindex from its registered PC, agreement = actual condition equals captured\nstatic bias, valid from the held conditional eligibility. The existing\nadvance input consumes it on MEM advancement. Remove the old EX-computed\ntrain outcome register: retaining it would preserve forwarded-comparator\nfanout and defeat the change. Preserve exactly the current training latency,\nreset saturation, aliasing policy and one update per legal aligned branch.\n\nMEM repair completes its owning instruction and kills both younger\npositions using the existing ID flush and EX control-only squash. Keep\nrepair priority over younger load/multiply/shift dependencies, unavailable\nimem and divider holds; suppress wrong-path DIV launch/completion, memory\ncontrols, training and later repair. Do not introduce recovery into wide\npayload data muxes, ordinary arithmetic registers or clock enables. Genuine\ndmem holds retain MEM source words and event metadata; consumption is once\nwhen MEM advances. Correct predictions still admit ready target fetches\nwithout bubbles. Preserve source forwarding, retained WB data and all\nother hazard schedules.\n\nForecast seven percent fitness gain with low confidence, entirely from\nFmax at unchanged marked cycles. This is initially an unmeasured timing\nhypothesis. The main risk is the new MEM full-comparison-to-squash cone\nbecoming critical; unchanged MEM multiplication may also cap timing.\nAcceptance above 234.39814 iter/sec requires median Gowin Fmax above\napproximately 103.52 MHz if cycles remain 4416239. Evaluate all three\nplacement options and actual marker-bounded CoreMark cycles together.\nPreserve nret=1, top-level IO, exact RV32IM results, decoder legality,\nalignment traps, RVFI operands/order, forward progress, canonical CRC/UART,\nmemory bounds, timing markers and every formal/cosim/evaluation check.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Remove all conditional comparisons from EX and resolve agree-prediction\nin MEM from existing EX/MEM source registers. Capture only event\neligibility, early polarity and bias; retain preselected repair targets\nand jump recovery. Generate exactly-once MEM training, preserving\ndownstream holds, control-only squash and divider behavior.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Complete conditional architectural successor and taken-target fault\nat MEM/WB from the owning MEM predicate. Keep deferred branch faults\nout of timed arithmetic/write-control paths. Preserve all memory\nrequests, alignment, multiplication, shifts and retained WB forwarding.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect the MEM conditional predicate to architectural completion\nif required, retaining existing redirect/squash and predictor update\nwiring. Preserve nret=1, all external ports and retirement order.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Adapt conditional checks to their MEM boundary without weakening\nexpected outcomes. Check all signed/unsigned predicates, capture/hold\nalignment, current-cycle recovery and training latency, while retaining\nnon-branch arithmetic, forwarding, jump, trap and divider assertions.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Verify all six predicates, byte/sign boundaries, taken/not-taken\nmisaligned targets, illegal encodings and both prediction outcomes.\nExercise bus holds, late dependencies, younger branches and wrong-path\nstores/DIV; assert resolved RVFI successors/traps/operands/orders,\nexactly-once training, unchanged recovery schedule and forward progress.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Replaced and schema-validated focused MEM prediction-validation hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
