lacement options and actual marker-bounded CoreMark cycles together.\nPreserve nret=1, top-level IO, exact RV32IM results, decoder legality,\nalignment traps, RVFI operands/order, forward progress, canonical CRC/UART,\nmemory bounds, timing markers and every formal/cosim/evaluation check.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Remove all conditional comparisons from EX and resolve agree-prediction\nin MEM from existing EX/MEM source registers. Capture only event\neligibility, early polarity and bias; retain preselected repair targets\nand jump recovery. Generate exactly-once MEM training, preserving\ndownstream holds, control-only squash and divider behavior.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Complete conditional architectural successor and taken-target fault\nat MEM/WB from the owning MEM predicate. Keep deferred branch faults\nout of timed arithmetic/write-control paths. Preserve all memory\nrequests, alignment, multiplication, shifts and retained WB forwarding.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect the MEM conditional predicate to architectural completion\nif required, retaining existing redirect/squash and predictor update\nwiring. Preserve nret=1, all external ports and retirement order.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Adapt conditional checks to their MEM boundary without weakening\nexpected outcomes. Check all signed/unsigned predicates, capture/hold\nalignment, current-cycle recovery and training latency, while retaining\nnon-branch arithmetic, forwarding, jump, trap and divider assertions.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Verify all six predicates, byte/sign boundaries, taken/not-taken\nmisaligned targets, illegal encodings and both prediction outcomes.\nExercise bus holds, late dependencies, younger branches and wrong-path\nstores/DIV; assert resolved RVFI successors/traps/operands/orders,\nexactly