    \"slack_ns\": -5.301,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 15.596,\n      \"logic_cells\": 9,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_divider\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Remove branch prediction comparator fanout into EX result eligibility',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. Predictor history was reviewed: the small agree\npredictor succeeded, while target tables and recovery retiming regressed.\nThe champion scores 224.09 iter/sec at 98.964 MHz and 4416239 marked\ncycles. Conditional branch resolution currently reaches not only prediction\nrepair/training but also EX trap, reg_write and fwd_ready through taken-\ntarget misalignment. A conditional branch has no register or memory result,\nso that target-fault control fanout is unnecessary for timed execution.\nIsolate it from result eligibility without changing prediction or repair.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing sixteen-counter agree predictor, folded PC index,\nstatic bias, direct B/J target arithmetic, balanced branch comparator,\nearly recovery polarity, training latency and registered MEM recovery.\nChange one aspect of predictor integration: the conditional comparator\nmust drive prediction outcome/recovery/training and architectural branch\nmetadata, but must not reach timed EX result eligibility via a branch\nalignment fault. Remove misalign_branch from the EX ctrl_with_trap\nis_illegal/reg_write overrides. Keep the complete misalign_jump override,\nincluding illegal reporting and link suppression, exactly as today.\n\nThis is safe because positively decoded conditional branches already have\nreg_write=0, mem_read=0 and mem_write=0, with ALU_ADD and no DIV request.\nTheir taken-target fault cannot suppress an architectural result that\nexists. Preserve the decoder's original is_illegal value, all controls\non illegal encodings, and the existing raw branch_taken/branch_target\nEX/MEM fields. Preserve full exact comparison, signed/unsigned handling\nand prediction mismatch in EX; do not move comparisons into MEM or\nintroduce another recovery cycle. The current alignment gate on recovery\nand training remains unchanged, so a misaligned branch target neither\nredirects nor trains. IF already predicts only aligned direct targets.\n\nAt the existing MEM/WB capture, add the conditional branch fault to the\nretiring is_illegal bit: owning EX/MEM ctrl.is_branch AND captured\nbranch_taken AND branch_target[1:0]\"'!=0. Keep this completion strictly on\nthe retirement trap path. It must not feed MEM multiplier/shift enables,\nload/store requests, reg_write, forwarding readiness, WB result selection\nor upstream stalls. The branch already has all those side effects disabled\nby decoding. No new source-value comparator or extra register is needed.\nDo not propagate the completed branch fault back to EX/MEM controls.\nKeep load/store misalignment and jump faults on their existing side-effect\nsuppression paths. This defers conditional trap reporting, never drops it.\n\nRetain EX'\"'s exact misalign_fault expression for architectural pc_next,\nwhich already chooses PC+4 on a taken misaligned branch. Its branch-only\nuse now feeds verification metadata, not timed eligibility. Taken aligned\nbranches report their target, untaken branches report PC+4 even when the\nunused target is misaligned, and a taken misaligned branch traps with\nPC+4. JAL/JALR retain current fault behavior and suppressed links. Capture\nthe completed branch trap only as the owning MEM instruction advances;\ndmem holds retain its record and retirement remains exactly once. RVFI\nsources, results, instruction, successor and contiguous order remain exact.\n\nKeep control-only EX squash, reset/hold rules, older registered recovery\npriority, divider request/result gating and younger training suppression.\nNo wrong-path instruction may regain eligibility after the fault-path\nchange. Add assertions that a decoded conditional branch never has any\nregister/memory side-effect control, and that its retirement trap matches\nthe exact captured taken-target fault plus original decoder legality.\nDo not assume those properties in formal or weaken existing tests.\n\nThe intended timing gain is reducing fanout on forwarded branch operands\nand eliminating the branch comparator's dependency into ctrl.reg_write,\nctrl.is_illegal, fwd_ready and divider metadata eligibility registers.\nThe champion's worst path is WB-to-EX ALU, so reducing nearby control and\nforwarding loading may improve that path even though arithmetic is fixed.\nForecast six percent fitness gain with low confidence at unchanged cycles.\nThe risk is that ordinary ALU/MEM multiplication still dominates and the\nfanout reduction does not clear the acceptance margin. Require measured\nfitness above 234.39814 iter/sec; at 4416239 cycles median Gowin Fmax must\nexceed about 103.52 MHz. Measure all three placement options and canonical\nmarker-bounded CoreMark, preserving every formal/cosim/CRC/UART/bounds\ncheck, nret=1, external IO, RV32IM arithmetic and forward progress.\n\nPrivate exploration rejected a full MEM branch-comparison probe (91.158\nMHz, option 0, unchanged 4416239 cycles and canonical CRCs) and direct\nfetch-target reuse (89.175 MHz, option 0). Neither is part of this proposal.\nA software replay found only 13735 returns and 46315 immediate-update\nagree misses, limiting accuracy-only upside. This final candidate isolates\nthe unnecessary conditional-fault fanout rather than enlarging prediction\nstate or moving the prediction comparison/recovery boundary.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Exclude only conditional target misalignment from EX trap/write/\nforwarding eligibility overrides. Preserve jump fault suppression,\noriginal decoder legality, exact comparator/recovery/training,\narchitectural pc_next, captured branch metadata and squash/divider\nrules. Assert branches already have no architectural side effects.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Complete the owning conditional taken-target fault only in MEM/WB's\nretirement is_illegal field from captured branch_taken/branch_target.\nKeep it out of timed requests, arithmetic enables, write eligibility,\nresult muxes and holds. Preserve memory alignment and every other\nretirement/writeback behavior.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Adjust conditional fault expectations to the retirement boundary,\nretaining exact EX pc_next and branch outcome checks. Verify branch\ncontrols stay side-effect-free and JAL/JALR faults still suppress links.\nKeep every arithmetic, forwarding, recovery, training and divider check.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Verify all six branch predicates with aligned and misaligned targets,\nboth taken outcomes, signed boundaries, illegal encodings, bus holds\nand older recovery squashes. Assert exact final traps/PCs/operands/orders,\nno wrong-path stores/DIV, unchanged cycles and exactly-once retirement.\nRetain existing decoder, alignment and liveness coverage.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261005-003-r14s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nprint('Final focused hypothesis written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
