{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(s)\n if '-r11s2' in r['id'] or '-r9s2' in r['id']:\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nprint('ELFS',list(Path('bench/programs').glob('*.elf')))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-003-r9s2\nImplement one stateless opcode-biased predictor for positively\nvalidated conditional branches: BEQ predicts not taken, BNE predicts\ntaken, and BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU predict backward taken and forward not\ntaken. For valid branch funct3 values the direction is exactly\ninstr[14] ? instr[31] : instr[12], a three-input Boolean function.\nAlso predict legal aligned JAL taken. Leave JALR on its existing\nforwarded resolution path. No branch PC, benchmark address, operand,\nmutable history or software annotation selects the static policy.\nExtract B/J immediates from\nraw imem data, calculate their exact full-width modulo-2^32 targets,\nand predict taken only if that target is word-aligned. Reserved branch\nfunct3 values and all non-direct instructions select PC+4. Store no\ntags, target entries, counters, validity arrays or training metadata.\n\nCarry only the actual selected predicted_taken bit through if_id_t\nand id_ex_t. Keep prediction decode and all wide payloads independent\nof redirect, flush and fetch validity. Capture this bit with the\nordinary instruction payload, holding it through true pipeline holds.\nAdvance fetch PC to the selected successor precisely when that same\ninstruction enters ID/EX as valid; imem stalls, load/multiply-use\nbubbles, older dmem freezes and divider waits consume no prediction.\n\nUse exact split-carry B/J target generation to bound fetch delay:\nbranch low12 addition and JAL low20 addition run beside upper-PC\nincrement/decrement candidates, followed by carry/sign selection.\nKeep all architectural address bits, correctly handle crossings and\nwraparound, and reject misaligned targets. Verify this construction\nagainst ordinary 32-bit addition before relying on it. Preserve the\nindependent PC+4 lane and original PC+4 link results.\n\nEX still computes architectural branch direction, targets, alignment\ntraps and RVFI pc_next from captured instruction/PC and forwarded\noperands. Since every predicted direct target was computed from that\nexact instruction, aligned conditional recovery requi\n…[7020 of 10092 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:16636be8ccfcd035]…\n counter write uses the captured agreement, not current fetch\nbits or a held/repeated branch. No predictor state or training target\nis added to divider metadata. Jumps, traps and bubbles never train.\n\nForecast a seven percent fitness improvement with low confidence.\nThe intended gain is better conditional accuracy and fewer harmful\ndirection aliases with a small state and recovery footprint. Protecting\nmedian Fmax is essential: prior predictors demonstrate that cycle\nreduction alone is insufficient. Measure actual marker-bounded\nCoreMark cycles and all three vendor placement options; require a\nscore greater than 209.05356 iter/sec. This forecast is unmeasured.\nPreserve the champion's arithmetic, effective-address lane, MEM\nmultiplier, unified WB result, registered forwarding matches,\nload/multiply interlock, retained MEM/WB forwarding and divider\nhandshakes. Keep nret=1, all top-level IO, exact RVFI retirement/order,\ndecoder legality, alignment traps and every invariant and evaluator\nfile unchanged.\n\nELFS []\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
