{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'imem|eval\\\\(|clock|stall' test/cosim/main.cpp -g '*.cpp'\"","aggregated_output":"25:static uint8_t imem[MEM_SIZE] = {};\n50:// ~22% stall). Replicating exactly so CoreMark/MHz numbers from this\n63:        std::cerr << \"usage: sim <elf> [maxcycles] [--bench] [--istall] [--dstall] [--seed N]\\n\";\n68:    // --istall: random ~22% imem-bus backpressure (VexRiscv-style).\n69:    // --dstall: same on dmem bus. The orchestrator's fitness eval\n74:    bool istall = false;\n75:    bool dstall = false;\n78:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--istall\") == 0) istall     = true;\n79:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--dstall\") == 0) dstall     = true;\n92:            memcpy(imem+vaddr, elf.data.data()+foff, filesz);\n99:    top->reset = 1; top->clock = 0;\n100:    top->io_imemReady = 1;\n102:    for(int i=0;i<5;i++){top->clock=0;top->eval();top->clock=1;top->eval();}\n114:        top->clock = 0;\n116:        // both imem and dmem when the corresponding flag is on. Drives 1\n118:        // slowed down by unrelated stalls.\n119:        top->io_imemReady = istall ? bus_accepts_main() : 1;\n120:        top->io_dmemReady = dstall ? bus_accepts_main() : 1;\n124:        //   - imem: PC should always be in range; flag every fetch outside.\n132:        //     in the dmem-write block below — kept BEFORE the clock posedge so\n135:        if (!in_mem_range(top->io_imemAddr)) oob_access = true;\n136:        top->io_imemData  = rw(imem, top->io_imemAddr);\n143:        top->eval();\n145:        // Process dmem writes BEFORE the clock posedge — see the matching\n177:        top->clock = 1; top->eval();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
