\"motivation\": \"The baseline predicts every control transfer as fall-through and flushes\\nthe younger fetched instruction for every taken branch, JAL, and JALR.\\nIF/ID is combinational, so this is a one-cycle recovery bubble, not the\\ntwo-cycle penalty of a pipeline with a separate IF/ID register. Repeated\\nCoreMark loops and calls should make many of these bubbles avoidable.\\nNo predictor attempts are recorded in the bench experiment history.\\nThe measured critical path runs through the combinational M-extension\\narithmetic; a small PC-indexed table should improve\n…[74459 of 77531 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19bb5349b59fdb61]…\nn\": \"Update packed bundle stimulus for prediction metadata and EX squash.\\nVerify both successors are registered without an EX recovery signal,\\nprediction metadata survives division and holds, squashed controls\\nare inert and divider launch cannot block an older MEM recovery.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 122.15, \"delta_pct\": -0.17, \"vs_baseline\": 907.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 52.294, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4281035, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3285, \"ff\": 1102, \"seeds\": [50.879, 52.294, 52.294], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.879, 13], [1, 52.294, 12], [2, 52.294, 12]], \"lutram\": 52, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.654, \"arrival_ns\": 24.949, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T00:57:07.584436Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
