{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'],d['category'],d['title'],'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'LUT',d.get('lut4'),'FF',d.get('ff'))\n if d['category']=='predictor' and 'r1s2' not in d['id'] and 'r4s2' not in d['id']:\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n print('notes:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-8c26bd0 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench fitness 12.12 MHz 5.442 cycles 4491485 LUT 12312 FF 460\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-001-r1s0 micro_opt Shared radix-4 combinational divider for RV32M fitness 13.23 MHz 5.944 cycles 4491485 LUT 5487 FF 460\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-002-r1s1 structural Move division out of the single-cycle execute path fitness 95.23 MHz 42.774 cycles 4491817 LUT 2617 FF 678\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-003-r1s2 predictor Small tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch hysteresis fitness 13.24 MHz 5.557 cycles 4197517 LUT 12641 FF 685\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-001-r2s0 micro_opt Remove redirect feedback from decode operand and hazard paths fitness 111.35 MHz 50.016 cycles 4491817 LUT 2502 FF 678\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-002-r2s1 structural Resolve control-flow redirects from the EX/MEM register fitness 107.09 MHz 51.943 cycles 4850577 LUT 2684 FF 780\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-003-r2s2 predictor Timing-aware tagged branch prediction on the iterative-divider core fitness 109.55 MHz 45.983 cycles 4197447 LUT 3059 FF 966\nAdd a single 64-entry direct-mapped tagged branch-target predictor to\nthe CURRENT iterative-divider core. Index by fetch PC[7:2], compare all\nremaining PC bits, and store an aligned full-width target, valid bit,\nconditional/unconditional bit, and two-bit saturating direction counter.\nA conditional hit predicts taken when its counter MSB is set; an\nunconditional hit predicts its last resolved target. A miss predicts\nPC+4. Allocate a conditional entry weakly toward the resolved outcome,\ntrain both outcomes, and refresh JAL/JALR targets when they resolve.\nUse only the registered PC for table lookup, with no instruction-memory\ndecode or operand forwarding in the prediction-to-PC path. Reset valid\nbits; allow invalid tag/target payloads to remain unreset and unobserved.\nDo not add global history, a return stack, caches, or arithmetic changes.\n\nMake prediction validation timing-aware. Carry predicted_taken and the\nexact selected target with the fetched instruction into ID. In ID,\nprecompute a\n…[7501 of 10573 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db0742f879b9ccfb]…\neasured cycle, a 6.86 percent rate\ngain at the champion clock. That is only an estimate: bus-stall\noverlap, speculative fetches and delayed counter training can change\nit. At that cycle estimate the 4.6 percent acceptance margin requires\napproximately 49.0 MHz; protecting Fmax is the main uncertainty.\nMeasure marked CoreMark\ncycles and median Gowin Fmax rather than treating cycle savings alone\nas success. Keep nret=1, all ports, decoder legality, architectural\nretirement data, and every existing formal/cosim/CRC/UART/marker gate.\n\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-001-r4s0 micro_opt Shorten EX operand delivery with registered dependency matches fitness 133.75 MHz 60.076 cycles 4491817 LUT 3303 FF 1613\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-002-r4s1 structural Separate the load/store address pipeline from ALU writeback fitness 129.49 MHz 58.164 cycles 4491817 LUT 2478 FF 710\nnotes: \nhyp-20261005-003-r4s2 predictor Validate cached next-PC predictions after the EX/MEM boundary fitness 122.15 MHz 52.294 cycles 4281035 LUT 3285 FF 1102\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
