{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r6s2.yaml; git status --short'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Carry-inferred micro-BTB target validation in parallel with branch resolution\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 150.99 at 67.824 MHz and 4491817 marked CoreMark\n  cycles. Earlier predictors removed roughly 290000 cycles but lost\n  clock rate; registered MEM recovery reduced that cycle benefit.\n  The latest instruction-validated target cache timed out on formal\n  pc_fwd rather than establishing correctness. LESSONS.md is absent.\n  The opportunity is a small predictor whose target correctness is\n  checked explicitly without an adder followed by an equality reduction.\n  This addresses the earlier timing and proof problems together.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one 16-entry direct-mapped micro-BTB to the current champion,\n  indexed by fetch PC[5:2]. Each entry holds a full remaining PC tag,\n  an aligned full-width target, valid and conditional/unconditional\n  type bits, and a two-bit saturating conditional direction counter.\n  Predict conditional branches from the counter MSB and JAL from their\n  cached target; misses predict PC+4. Leave JALR unpredicted. Allocate\n  conditional entries\n  weakly toward the resolved outcome. Reset valid bits only.\n\n  Implement each entry as an independently declared register bank with\n  constant-index writes. Decode the fetch index into one-hot enables,\n  compare that entry's complete PC tag locally, and gate its target\n  by its valid, tag-hit and taken state. OR the mutually exclusive\n  target terms with a balanced tree. Avoid a priority encoder, a\n  dynamically indexed packed target array, and instruction-memory\n  validation on the prediction-to-PC path. Full tags, including any\n  non-index low PC bits, must distinguish every architectural PC.\n  This deliberately small lookup is the predictor's timing hypothesis.\n\n  Carry predicted_taken and the exact selected target with each accepted\n  fetch into ID/EX. In EX, validate the untrusted cached direct target\n  with a parallel addition checker instead of calculating an addition\n  and then c\n…[8090 of 11162 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:41f1fb1a5f575966]…\neplacement, conditional destinations, JALR exclusion,\n      one-hot selection and exactly-once accepted updates.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise warmed loops and exits, stale targets on changed\n      instructions, back-to-back transfers, JAL/JALR links and alignment\n      traps under both bus stalls and divider holds. Check exact RVFI\n      operands, successors, contiguous orders and no wrong-path effects.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Update packed-bundle stimulus and check direct target/direction\n      repair, unpredicted JALR redirects, non-control stale predictions,\n      alignment traps and held prediction/divider metadata.\n  - file: test/test_target_checker.py\n    description: |\n      Check equality with modulo-2^32 PC-plus-immediate for positive\n      and negative B/J displacements, wraparound, long carry/borrow\n      patterns and deliberately wrong targets. Exercise arbitrary\n      32-bit vectors as well; do not constrain predictor targets.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
