{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261005-003-r3s2':\n  print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k not in ('hypothesis','changes')},indent=2))\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261005-003-r3s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Instruction-qualified direction prediction without a target table\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion already removes redirect from raw fetch/decode payloads\\nand reaches 111.35 iterations/second at 50.016 MHz. The previous\\n64-entry tagged predictor reduced marked CoreMark cycles from\\n4491817 to 4197447, but its 45.983 MHz clock erased the gain. Its\\ncritical path crossed EX recovery, IF, immediate decoding, and the\\nID direct_target_match register. Recovering predictable direct-control\\nbubbles is worthwhile only if prediction avoids that feedback cone.\\nA reference-ISS profile of the canonical -O3, 2K, 10-iteration ELF\\nbetween its MMIO markers found 294425 taken conditional branches,\\n49367 JALs, and only 13735 JALRs. A 32-entry direction-table replay\\nproduced 55558 conditional misses, removing 288234 net control bubbles\\nin this software model while leaving JALR unpredicted. The UART had\\nthe canonical five CRCs and the validation literal. These are trace\\nstatistics, not a measured RTL cycle count or Gowin fitness result.\\nThere is no LESSONS.md in this fixture. Both prior predictor outcomes\\nwere reviewed in experiments/log.jsonl before selecting this approach.\\n\",\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 108.92,\n  \"delta_pct\": -2.18,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 798.68,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 45.786,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 4203461,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 2811,\n  \"ff\": 804,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    47.258,\n    45.786,\n    45.786\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      47.258,\n      17\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      45.786,\n      16\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      45.786,\n      16\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 8,\n  \"bsram\": 6,\n  \"dsp\": 6,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -16.161,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 26.455,\n    \"logic_cells\": 19,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_e\n…[3393 of 6465 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fe61cd33ce58067a]…\nh, saturating up/down on its actual\noutcome; do not update for jumps, bubbles, traps, or repeated hold\ncycles. Preserve the iterative divider and MEM/WB forwarding retention.\n\nThe forecast is a 7 percent fitness gain from direct-control bubble\nremoval with approximately unchanged Fmax. Omitting JALR prediction\ntrades some cycle benefit for a much smaller prediction/recovery cone.\nThe software replay suggests approximately 4203583 cycles if each net\nbubble removed translated to one measured cycle, a 6.86 percent rate\ngain at the champion clock. That is only an estimate: bus-stall\noverlap, speculative fetches and delayed counter training can change\nit. At that cycle estimate the 4.6 percent acceptance margin requires\napproximately 49.0 MHz; protecting Fmax is the main uncertainty.\nMeasure marked CoreMark\ncycles and median Gowin Fmax rather than treating cycle savings alone\nas success. Keep nret=1, all ports, decoder legality, architectural\nretirement data, and every existing formal/cosim/CRC/UART/marker gate.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
