{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261005-003-r3s2','hyp-20261005-003-r6s2','hyp-20261005-003-r7s2'):\n  h=r['hypothesis']['hypothesis']\n  n=h.find('replay')\n  print('\\\\n',r['id'],h[max(0,n-200):][-4500:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261005-003-r3s2 percent fitness gain from direct-control bubble\nremoval with approximately unchanged Fmax. Omitting JALR prediction\ntrades some cycle benefit for a much smaller prediction/recovery cone.\nThe software replay suggests approximately 4203583 cycles if each net\nbubble removed translated to one measured cycle, a 6.86 percent rate\ngain at the champion clock. That is only an estimate: bus-stall\noverlap, speculative fetches and delayed counter training can change\nit. At that cycle estimate the 4.6 percent acceptance margin requires\napproximately 49.0 MHz; protecting Fmax is the main uncertainty.\nMeasure marked CoreMark\ncycles and median Gowin Fmax rather than treating cycle savings alone\nas success. Keep nret=1, all ports, decoder legality, architectural\nretirement data, and every existing formal/cosim/CRC/UART/marker gate.\n\n\n hyp-20261005-003-r6s2 cker neither\nfollows an adder nor lengthens the imem-to-ID payload path.\nNo formal assumptions may constrain instructions, predictor state\nor memory to make this proposal pass.\n\nA fresh reference-ISS replay of the canonical ELF between MMIO markers\nrecorded 2922016 instructions and 357527 taken control transfers,\nincluding 13735 unpredicted JALR transfers. The chosen 16-entry direct\ntable with taken-only allocation had 67510 direct successor misses\nand saved a net 276282 bubbles. Charging one cycle per net bubble\ngives 4215535 estimated cycles and a 6.554 percent rate gain at\nunchanged clock. Allocating on both branch outcomes instead saved\n257288 bubbles: avoiding not-taken miss allocation saves a further\n18994 cycles with no additional table bits. The chosen 16-entry table\nalso slightly exceeds the earlier 32-entry allocate-both-outcomes\nreplay's 272597 saved bubbles despite having half as many entries.\nWith the same taken-only policy, 32 entries saved 289623 bubbles,\nonly 13341 more than 16 entries, about 0.32 percent extra throughput\nat unchanged clock. Retain 16 entries to favor timing and proof size.\nThe replay produced all five canonical CRCs, ITE\n…[4365 of 7437 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:20fb4746f1afa1f9]…\ne also passed\nfull retirement-trace cosim for selftest and random1/2/3, each with\nzero wait and with both bus stalls. An independent Yosys SAT proof\nestablished the inferred-carry equality for arbitrary 32-bit operands\nand for the constant-four case. These are hypothesis-generation probe\nresults, not a substitute for the implementation phase's gates.\n\nForecast a rounded 5 percent fitness gain with low confidence because\nthe acceptance margin is narrow. At 4251084 cycles acceptance requires\nmedian Fmax above 77.01570 MHz, just 0.40 percent below the measured\n77.325 MHz. Preserve the exact small table, registered training and\nshared architectural successor path. Predictor placement and the\nlive-PC-check-to-recovery cone are the principal remaining risks.\nMeasure marked cycles and median vendor Fmax after implementation;\ncycle savings alone do not establish success. The design focuses on\none direct predictor and its validation, with no arithmetic, memory,\npipeline-depth, global-history or return-stack changes.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
